      "issue_type": "Missing File Extension Validation",
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "t61.py",
      "line": 11,
      "evidence": "The code does not validate the file extension, allowing potentially executable files to be uploaded if they spoof the content-type.",
      "llm_reasoning": "Even with content-type checks, an attacker can bypass filters if the extension is not strictly validated against a whitelist.",
      "suggested_fix": "Validate the file extension using os.path.splitext(file.filename) against a list of allowed extensions."
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The code contained critical security vulnerabilities including path traversal and memory exhaustion risks, alongside poor architectural practices. The refactored code implements streaming I/O, path sanitization, and improved configuration management to ensure production readiness.",
  "fixed_code": "import os\nimport aiofiles\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, File, HTTPException, UploadFile\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\napp = FastAPI()\nUPLOAD_DIR = Path(os.getenv(\"UPLOAD_DIR\", \"/var/app/uploads\"))\nMAX_BYTES = 5 * 1024 * 1024\nALLOWED_TYPES = {\"image/png\", \"image/jpeg\"}\nALLOWED_EXTENSIONS = {\".png\", \".jpg\", \".jpeg\"}\n\nasync def save_avatar(file: UploadFile) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Validates and saves an avatar image to the server.\"\"\"\n    filename = Path(file.filename).name\n    if Path(filename).suffix.lower() not in ALLOWED_EXTENSIONS:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=\"Invalid file extension\")\n    \n    dest = UPLOAD_DIR / filename\n    async with aiofiles.open(dest, \"wb\") as fh:\n        while chunk := await file.read(1024 * 64):\n            await fh.write(chunk)\n    return filename\n\n@app.post(\"/avatars\")\nasync def upload_avatar(file: UploadFile = File(...)) -> dict[str, str | int]:\n    if file.content_type not in ALLOWED_TYPES:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=415, detail=\"unsupported type\")\n    \n    # Check size without loading full file into memory\n    file.file.seek(0, os.SEEK_END)\n    size = file.file.tell()\n    file.file.seek(0)\n    if size > MAX_BYTES:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=413, detail=\"file too large\")\n\n    stored_name = await save_avatar(file)\n    return {\"stored_as\": stored_name, \"bytes\": size}"
}
